# Slice 307 (CALL-WHOLE-ARGUMENTS-STRUCTURE; the review of Codex, item 4): a Structure field of a whole call is admitted at its
# formal by the first part of implements -- the Consumer's uses of the formal projected into the field's model
# (lm_compiler_whole_applicable).  g (Point: p; int: q) reads p\x and p\y; BArgs (Bad: p; int: q 7) names g's formals, but
# Bad (int: x 1) has no y: the translation refuses the call, "implements is false in function argument".
Point:
    int: x 1
    int: y 2
end: Point
Bad:
    int: x 1
end: Bad
BArgs:
    Bad: p
    int: q 7
end: BArgs
fn: g (Point: p; int: q) int
    return: p\x + p\y + q
end: g
fn: run () int
    return: g(BArgs)
end: run
int: code run()
send: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
